<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT MUST STAY INSIDE THE ROOT <Flow> ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        Mirrors NDA_Signed_Status_Sync, with two deliberate differences:

        1) Keys on Stage__c, not LOI_Status__c. Stage__c is the field the Advance Stage button and
           the Path actually write (LoiSelector.cls:121-123 documents why the two are not to be
           coupled); LOI_Status__c is a separate approval/deal vocabulary field that no automation
           ever sets to 'Signed'. Acquisition_LOI's Stage__c sequence ends at 'Signed' (terminal);
           Disposition_LOI's terminal is the distinct value 'Executed', so this flow is naturally
           Acquisition-only with no record-type criterion needed (2026-08-18 design decision D1/D2).

        2) THE Is_Signed DECISION HAS NO FALSE/DEFAULT CONNECTOR, AND THERE IS NO Set_Signed_False
           ASSIGNMENT AT ALL - NOT EVEN AN UNCONNECTED ONE. DO NOT ADD ONE. NDA_Signed_Status_Sync
           carries an unconnected Set_Signed_False assignment that its own in-root comment (added
           2026-08-16) flags as a hazard for exactly this reason: an unconnected assignment sitting
           in a flow's canvas invites a future editor to "finish the job" by wiring it up, which
           would un-sign LOIs on every stage move away from 'Signed'. This flow avoids that trap
           entirely by never defining the assignment in the first place. The checkbox is a one-way
           latch: once Stage__c reaches 'Signed', LOI_Signed__c stays true forever, even if the LOI
           is later reopened or its stage otherwise changes.

        3) LOI_Signed_Notify (force-app/main/default/flows/LOI_Signed_Notify.flow-meta.xml), an
           AFTER-SAVE flow keyed on LOI_Signed__c = true, is being DEACTIVATED in this same change
           (see that file's in-root comment and its paired FlowDefinition). Without deactivating it,
           this flow would make LOI_Signed_Notify fire its Legal_Team and Investor_Relations
           GroupNotifier calls automatically on every ordinary Acquisition LOI stage advance to
           'Signed' - a real behaviour change into Legal/IR that was explicitly NOT wanted when this
           latch was introduced (2026-08-18 design decision D3). Reactivating LOI_Signed_Notify
           without re-reviewing this consequence would silently restore that unwanted behaviour.
    -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Signed_True</name>
        <label>Set Signed True</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.LOI_Signed__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Needs_Signed_Date</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Stamp_Signed_Date</name>
        <label>Stamp Signed Date</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>504</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.LOI_Signed_Date__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Flow.CurrentDate</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Signed</name>
        <label>Is Signed?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>180</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Signed</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Stage_Is_Signed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Stage__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Signed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Signed_True</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Signed</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Needs_Signed_Date</name>
        <label>Needs Signed Date?</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>396</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Already set</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Signed_Date_Is_Blank</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.LOI_Signed_Date__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Stamp_Signed_Date</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Stamp</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Derives LOI_Signed__c from Stage__c on every save, in ONE direction only: Stage__c = &apos;Signed&apos; sets the checkbox true. It never sets it false for any other Stage - there is no false/default connector and no Set_Signed_False-style assignment at all, so the checkbox latches true once set. Also stamps LOI_Signed_Date__c to TODAY() the first time Stage__c reaches &apos;Signed&apos; with a blank date - never overwrites an existing date and never clears it when Stage__c moves away. Before-save so any validation or automation reading LOI_Signed__c sees the synced value in the same transaction. Acquisition-only by construction: Disposition_LOI&apos;s terminal Stage__c value is &apos;Executed&apos;, not &apos;Signed&apos;. See the in-root XML comment in this file before adding a false branch, and see LOI_Signed_Notify.flow-meta.xml (deactivated in this same change) before reactivating that flow.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>LOI Signed Status Sync {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>LOI Signed Status Sync</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Is_Signed</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <object>LOI__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordBeforeSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
